---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Cta from '../components/Cta.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import { SITE, SOCIALS } from '../site';
import { langOf, lp } from '../i18n';

const lang = langOf(Astro.url.pathname);
const pt = lang === 'pt';
const n = (await getCollection('certifications', (c) => c.data.status === 'earned')).length;
const yt = SOCIALS.find((s) => s.label === 'YouTube')!.href;
const htb = SOCIALS.find((s) => s.label === 'HackTheBox')!.href;
const thm = SOCIALS.find((s) => s.label === 'TryHackMe')!.href;
// CTF stats, from the public profiles on 2026-11-22. Hours: TryHackMe's own estimated time
// per completed room (~119 h) + HTB machines at ~3/6/10/16 h for Easy/Medium/Hard/Insane
// (26/12/4/1 → ~206 h). Update these when the profiles change.
const HTB_MACHINES = 43;
const THM_ROOMS = 138;
const LAB_HOURS = 300;
const aiLabs = (await getCollection('ai', (e) => !e.data.draft)).length;
const mail = `mailto:${SITE.email}`;

const career = pt
  ? [
      { when: 'nov 2026 — atual', what: 'Pesquisador de segurança independente', note: 'Projetos de pentest, bug bounty e pesquisa de vulnerabilidades em software open source.' },
      { when: '2026', what: 'Cybersecurity Lead · Sietch.tech', note: 'Liderei o time de pentest e fui responsável pela infraestrutura de segurança.' },
      { when: '2025 — 2026', what: 'Analista de SOC · iT.eam', note: 'Engenharia de detecção, triagem de alertas e resposta a incidentes.' },
      { when: 'Antes', what: 'Analista de NOC · K2 Telecom', note: 'Operação e monitoramento de redes.' },
    ]
  : [
      { when: 'Nov 2026 — now', what: 'Independent security researcher', note: 'Penetration testing engagements, bug bounty and open-source vulnerability research.' },
      { when: '2026', what: 'Cybersecurity Lead · Sietch.tech', note: 'Led the pentest team and owned the security infrastructure.' },
      { when: '2025 — 2026', what: 'SOC Analyst · iT.eam', note: 'Detection engineering, alert triage and incident response.' },
      { when: 'Earlier', what: 'NOC Analyst · K2 Telecom', note: 'Network operations and monitoring.' },
    ];
---
<Base
  title={pt ? 'Sobre' : 'About'}
  active="about"
  description={pt
    ? 'Sobre Giulliano Amaral — pentester e pesquisador de segurança ofensiva no Rio de Janeiro.'
    : 'About Giulliano Amaral — penetration tester and offensive security researcher based in Rio de Janeiro.'}
>
  <header class="pagehead">
    <p class="kicker">whoami</p>
    <h1>Giulliano <em>Amaral</em></h1>
  </header>

  <section class="about">
    <img class="about__photo" src="/portrait.jpg" alt={pt ? 'Retrato de Giulliano Amaral' : 'Portrait of Giulliano Amaral'} width="560" height="750" />
    <div class="about__body">
      {pt ? (
        <>
          <p>
            Sou <strong>pentester e pesquisador de segurança ofensiva</strong> no Rio de Janeiro.
            Já atuei dos dois lados: em um SOC, analisando alertas e respondendo a incidentes, e à frente de um time de pentest.
            Ter visto os ataques pela perspectiva de quem defende influencia a forma como eu testo e como documento cada achado.
          </p>
          <p>
            Trabalho principalmente com <strong>aplicações web e APIs</strong>, <strong>Active Directory</strong> e, cada vez mais, <strong>sistemas de IA/LLM</strong> e os agentes construídos sobre eles.
            Fora dos projetos, procuro vulnerabilidades em software open source e compartilho o que aprendo aqui e no <a href={yt}>YouTube</a>.
          </p>
          <p>
            Mantenho a prática em dia com CTFs: <strong>{HTB_MACHINES} máquinas no HackTheBox</strong> e <strong>{THM_ROOMS} salas no TryHackMe</strong>, somando mais de {LAB_HOURS} horas de laboratório.
            No <a href={htb}>HackTheBox</a>, estou no rank Pro Hacker e já cheguei ao <strong>top 80 do ranking brasileiro</strong>, além de disputar as temporadas competitivas.
            No <a href={thm}>TryHackMe</a>, estou entre os <strong>2% melhores do mundo</strong>.
            Também resolvi {aiLabs} desafios das trilhas Advanced e Expert do Arkx AI Red-Team CTF, voltado a ataques contra agentes de IA.
          </p>
          <p>
            Sou pós-graduado em Red Team e tenho <a href={lp(lang, '/certs/')}>{n} certificações práticas em segurança ofensiva</a>.
            Falo português, inglês, espanhol e japonês (日本語). Para falar comigo, escreva para <a href={mail}>{SITE.email}</a>.
          </p>
        </>
      ) : (
        <>
          <p>
            I'm a <strong>penetration tester and offensive security researcher</strong> based in Rio de Janeiro.
            I've worked on both sides: in a SOC, triaging alerts and responding to incidents, and as the lead
            of a pentest team. Having seen how attacks look from the defender's seat shapes how I test and
            how I write findings up.
          </p>
          <p>
            My work focuses on <strong>web applications and APIs</strong>, <strong>Active Directory</strong>
            and, increasingly, <strong>AI/LLM systems</strong> and the agents built on them. Outside client work
            I hunt bugs in open-source software and publish what I learn here and on <a href={yt}>YouTube</a>.
          </p>
          <p>
            I keep my skills sharp with CTFs: <strong>{HTB_MACHINES} HackTheBox machines</strong> and <strong>{THM_ROOMS} TryHackMe rooms</strong>, more than {LAB_HOURS} hours of hands-on labs.
            On <a href={htb}>HackTheBox</a> I've reached the <strong>top 80 in
            Brazil</strong>, at the Pro Hacker rank, and I play the competitive seasons.
            On <a href={thm}>TryHackMe</a> I'm in the <strong>top 2% worldwide</strong>.
            I also solved {aiLabs} Advanced and Expert challenges in the Arkx AI Red-Team CTF, which focuses on attacking AI agents.
          </p>
          <p>
            I hold a postgraduate degree in Red Team operations and <a href={lp(lang, '/certs/')}>{n} hands-on offensive certifications</a>.
            I speak Portuguese, English, Spanish and Japanese (日本語). You can reach me at <a href={mail}>{SITE.email}</a>.
          </p>
        </>
      )}
      <div class="btnrow" style="margin-top:24px;">
        {SOCIALS.map((s) => <a class="btn btn--ghost btn--sm" href={s.href} rel="me noopener" target="_blank">{s.label} ↗</a>)}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section__head"><div><p class="kicker">cat experience.log</p><h2>{pt ? 'Experiência' : 'Experience'}</h2></div></div>
    <div class="timeline">
      {career.map((c) => (
        <div class="tl">
          <div class="tl__when">{c.when}</div>
          <div><div class="tl__what">{c.what}</div><p class="tl__note">{c.note}</p></div>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section__head">
      <div>
        <p class="kicker">cat ethics.md</p>
        {pt ? (
          <>
            <h2>Regras de <em>engajamento</em></h2>
            <p>
              Só testo sistemas com autorização por escrito do responsável, e achados de clientes nunca são publicados.
              Os writeups deste site cobrem máquinas já aposentadas do HackTheBox e plataformas de laboratório; os de máquinas ativas ficam protegidos por senha.
              Vulnerabilidades em projetos open source só são divulgadas depois que os mantenedores publicam a correção.
            </p>
          </>
        ) : (
          <>
            <h2>Rules of <em>engagement</em></h2>
            <p>
              I only test systems with written authorization from their owner. Client findings are never published.
              The writeups here cover retired HackTheBox machines and lab platforms; writeups for active machines
              are sealed. Vulnerabilities in open-source projects are disclosed only after the maintainers publish a fix.
            </p>
          </>
        )}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Cta />
</Base>
